From 02893efe4ef5deccbf17393cfa83f337295397be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:46:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] metal: union the dropped upstream FA machinery back in - the
 tree did not compile

The 2026-08-29 policy ("in a conflicting hunk of an off-rig backend file the fork
side wins, upstream's change is DROPPED") was reversed by the President on
2026-09-06: a public engine that claims to ingest everything cannot silently lag
upstream on CUDA/Metal/SYCL. This is the first repair under the new rule, and the
Metal tree turns out not to be a matter of policy at all - it does not build.

CHECKED at 697027562, five function DEFINITIONS are absent while their callers,
their declarations, or both survive:

  ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_use_kv_f16      called by extra_pad (upstream form)
  ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_v_is_view_of_k  called by extra_kv_f16
  ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_kv_f16_k_size   called by extra_kv_f16
  ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_extra_kv_f16    DECLARED in ggml-metal-ops.h and
                                               CALLED from ggml-metal.cpp:240
  ggml_metal_op_flash_attn_ext_n_kv_max_sparse CALLED from extra_idx:3346

and ggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_flash_attn_ext_kv_f16 is declared in
ggml-metal-device.h with no definition in ggml-metal-device.cpp. Both FA pipeline
getters are declared in that header with (use_kv_f16, ns10, ns20) and defined
without them, and the vec call site passes 9 of the 12 arguments its own
definition takes. The sparse dispatch at 3604-3952 reads use_sparse,
n_kv_max_sparse, n_kv_max_padded and bid_idx, none of which is declared in that
scope. Nothing here is a judgement call; this is a half-applied merge on the one
backend the estate cannot compile, which is why nothing caught it.

RESOLUTION - hand union, upstream's form carrying our mechanism. The FA op
function is rebuilt from upstream b10819 6a1a922d2 with every ArifiLabs mechanism
re-inserted, so no line of either side is lost:

  ours, carried     asymmetric K/V type assertion (turbo / q8_0 mixed pairs)
  ours, carried     TurboFlash two-pass dispatch, byte-identical, same insertion
                    point, still returning early
  ours, carried     TurboQuant +128-float threadgroup block cache in FATTN_SMEM
  ours, carried     asymmetric k%s_v%s pipeline naming in both getters
  theirs, restored  KV-F16 dequant pass and its nb*_attn stride threading
  theirs, restored  MLA v_is_view_of_k (dequantized V is a view of dequantized K)
  theirs, restored  sparse index-list path, whose callers already survived
  theirs, restored  fa_vec_pick tuning (nqptg) - ggml-metal-tuning.cpp is 3856
                    lines of tuned table at the tip with ZERO call sites
  theirs, restored  qne_suffix in the vec pipeline name - without it two
                    different (nqpsg, ne) tunings hash to the SAME cached
                    pipeline, because neither value appears elsewhere in the key

R13 collision #7 recorded the Metal sparse-FA as "structurally exclusive with our
TurboFlash at this insertion point". CHECKED: they are not. TurboFlash gates on
V = turbo3 with single-token decode; the sparse path's own type switch admits only
F16/BF16/F32/Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q8_0. The gates are disjoint, so both paths
coexist and the default for a model without our types is exactly upstream's
behaviour. #7 is closed as a union, not as a keep-ours.

Loss control: brace/paren balance is identical to BOTH parents (2, -5), which is
the R13B control - a file matching neither parent is the signal. Every identifier
in the rebuilt function resolves within the function or the Metal tree.

NOT VERIFIED, and it cannot be here: this estate has no Metal toolchain. This is
union-by-mechanism-read; compile verification is PENDING the first run of the
macos-latest job in .github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml. It is not
benched and no performance claim is made.

Origin: upstream llama.cpp b10819 (6a1a922d2), PR #27390 + PR #13435, unioned with ArifiLabs TurboFlash / TurboQuant / asymmetric-KV
WI: WI-1698
Lane: lane-210
